es not validate the index.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'record', 'value': 'new Record(Name.fromString("bad.example."), Type.TXT, DClass.IN, 0, new TXTRecord(Name.fromString("bad.example."), DClass.IN, 0, "bad"))'}, {'parameter': 'section', 'value': 'Message.sections.length'}], 'expected': 'ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException is thrown', 'description': 'Passing an index equal to the length of the sections array (out of upper bound) should also result in an ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException.'}]}, {'group': 'addRecord – null Record argument', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'record', 'value': 'null'}, {'parameter': 'section', 'value': 'Message.SECTION_QUESTION'}], 'expected': 'NullPointerException is thrown when trying to add a null record to the list', 'description': 'The method does not guard against a null Record; attempting to add it should cause a NullPointerException from the List implementation.'}]}, {'group': 'addRecord – multiple records in same section (cumulative header count)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'record', 'value': 'new Record(Name.fromString("example.com."), Type.A, DClass.IN, 3600, InetAddress.getByName("192.0.2.1"))'}, {'parameter': 'section', 'value': 'Message.SECTION_ANSWER'}], 'expected': 'Header.incCount(Message.SECTION_ANSWER) is called once; answer count becomes 1; sections[Message.SECTION_ANSWER] contains the record.', 'description': 'First addition to an empty answer section creates the list and increments the header count to 1.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'record', 'value': 'new Record(Name.fromString("example.org."), Type.AAAA, DClass.IN, 7200, InetAddress.getByName("2001:db8::1"))'}, {'parameter': 'section', 'value': 'Message.SECTION_ANSWER'}], 'expected': 'Header.incCount(Message.SECTION_ANSWER) is called again; answer count becomes 2; sections[Message.SECTION_ANSWER] now contains both records in insertion order.', 'description': 'Adding a second record to the same answer section should not create a new list, should append the record, and the header count should reflect the total number of records.'}]}, {'group': 'addRecord – adding to QUESTION section (single‑question semantics)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'record', 'value': 'new Record(Name.fromString("lookup.example."), Type.A, DClass.IN, 0, null)'}, {'parameter': 'section', 'value': 'Message.SECTION_QUESTION'}], 'expected': 'Header.incCount(Message.SECTION_QUESTION) is called once; sections[Message.SECTION_QUESTION] contains exactly the supplied record; subsequent calls with another question record increase the list size (even though typical usage expects only one).', 'description': 'Verify that addRecord works for the QUESTION section, increments the question count, and stores the record even though DNS messages normally contain a single question.'}]}, {'group': 'addRecord – header field is null (NullPointerException)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'record', 'value': 'new Record(Name.fromString("nullheader.example."), Type.SOA, DClass.IN, 0, new SOARecord(Name.fromString("nullheader.example."), DClass.IN, 3600, Name.fromString("ns.example."), Name.fromString("hostmaster.example."), 2021010101L, 7200, 3600, 1209600, 3600))'}, {'parameter': 'section', 'value': 'Message.SECTION_AUTHORITY'}], 'expected': 'NullPointerException is thrown because Message.header is null and addRecord attempts to call header.incCount(section).', 'description': 'The method does not guard against a null Header; forcing header to null should cause a NPE when incCount is invoked.'}]}, {'group': 'addRecord – pre‑populated section with a different List implementation', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'record', 'value': 'new Record(Name.fromString("arraylist.example."), Type.NS, DClass.IN, 300, new NSRecord(Name.fromString("arraylist.example."), DClass.IN, 300, Name.fromString("ns1.example.")))'}, {'parameter': 'section', 'value': 'Message.SECTION_ADDITIONAL'}], 'expected': 'The existing ArrayList instance in sections[Message.SECTION_ADDITIONAL] is reused (no new LinkedList created); the record is appended; Header.incCount(Message.SECTION_ADDITIONAL) is called once and count increments by 1.', 'description': 'If a section is already initialized with a List that is not a LinkedList (e.g., an ArrayList), addRecord should still add the record without replacing the List.'}]}, {'group': 'addRecord – maximum valid section index (SECTION_ADDITIONAL) boundary test', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'record', 'value': 'new Record(Name.fromString("boundary.example."), Type.CNAME, DClass.IN, 0, new CNAMERecord(Name.fromString("boundary.example."), DClass.IN, 0, Name.fromString("target.example.")))'}, {'parameter': 'section', 'value': 'Message.SECTION_ADDITIONAL'}], 'expected': 'Header.incCount(Message.SECTION_ADDITIONAL) is called once; sections[Message.SECTION_ADDITIONAL] contains the record; no exception is thrown.', 'description': 'Confirm that the highest defined section index is accepted and processed correctly.'}]}]
